1904–05 was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 17th season of competitive football. They competed in the [[Scottish First Division]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1900/celtic1905.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1904-05|website=Londonhearts.com|accessdate=9 August 2018}}</ref> which they won for the first time since 1897-98. It was Celtic's 5th league title and 9th major title overall.

Celtic and [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] had finished the league campaign level on 41 points, and a play-off at [[Hampden Park]] (doubling up as a fixture in the minor [[Glasgow Football League]]) was arranged to decide the championship. An English-based referee was drafted in to officiate at the match due to increasing tensions between the two groups of supporters and controversies in recent matches between the sides. Celtic won 2–1, with [[Jimmy McMenemy]] and [[Davie Hamilton]] scoring the decisive goals.

Celtic also won the [[Glasgow Charity Cup]].

